              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "No answers yet. Start studying to track progress. Use the same Home layout and all 13 group rows; every action is Study group. These are the only changed regions.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mDXHv",
          "name": "Cross-screen implementation contract",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Shared screen rules: use the Home palette, 8 px controls, 48 px primary actions and Inter typography. Main pages use 32 px desktop/tablet headings and 28 px mobile headings; German question prompts use 28 / 24 px. Supporting reading text is at least 14 px; 12 px is reserved for navigation, compact status and metadata. Preserve German source content in both interface languages.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ClY7Y",
          "name": "Modal and validation implementation contract",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Dialogs are viewport overlays: 520 px on desktop, viewport width minus 40 px on mobile. Initial focus is the safe action (Open question list, Stay in test, or Cancel), with a focus trap and Escape restoration. Date errors appear after blur or save, preserve the typed value, and leave the saved date unchanged. Import failure keeps local data untouched; submitting actions block duplicate activation.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "qKG9Y",
          "name": "Supportive feedback heading",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Supportive feedback · shared interaction contract",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-20",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "t4TrPx",
          "name": "Study acknowledgment",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "On a submitted study answer changing Learning → Learned, show Correct — now marked Learned and Two correct answers in a row. Other correct answers show Correct. Keep acknowledgment with the session answer on back/forward navigation, without replay or announcement; clear it with session feedback. New feedback is announced politely once. Do not move focus, auto-advance, or delay controls. Mock grading changes status without individual milestone announcements.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kFrJ8",
          "name": "Translation and recovery",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "When English study translation is on, repeat the bank’s correct-answer English translation below the German correction. Hide that line when translation is off or UI language is German. Failed results keep score, threshold, unanswered count and finish reason, then offer review guidance; use below only in stacked layouts. Passing results show Mock test passed, the actual score, a check and Well done. No real-test guarantee.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Z7DKm",
          "name": "Completion and repetition",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Completion acknowledges reaching the group’s end, not mastery or 100% progress. Keep the check beside the heading, separate from the exact progress fraction. Review starts another pass and preserves history. All added treatments are static; no sound, confetti, streaks, toasts or reduced-motion dependency. Retain keyboard focus, 48 px controls and wrapping copy.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "L5k8l",
          "name": "Localization wording",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "German: Du hast das Ende dieser Gruppe erreicht. / Gut, dass du dir Zeit zum Üben genommen hast. / Richtig — jetzt als Gelernt markiert / Zweimal in Folge richtig beantwortet. / Weiter bei Frage {position} von {total} / Probetest bestanden / Gut gemacht. Complete EN/DE copy is specified in docs/requirements.md, Supportive feedback and completion.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "AAloB",
          "name": "Study help · expanded state reference",
          "context": "Default screens show this disclosure collapsed. Expanding adds this copy below its 44 px trigger; preserve focus, current answer and scroll access. German label: So funktioniert Lernen. German body: Beantworte jede Frage einmal pro Lernsitzung. Vorherige und Nächste behalten deine Antworten und Rückmeldungen bei. Starte eine neue Lernsitzung oder öffne eine Frage unter Fortschritt, um erneut zu antworten. Frühere Versuche und gespeicherte Positionen bleiben erhalten.",
          "width": 700,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$spacing-8",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "yJsKf",
              "name": "How study works · expanded trigger",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 44,
              "gap": "$spacing-8",
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "icon",
                  "id": "cGGcO",
                  "name": "Collapse study help",
                  "width": 18,
                  "height": 18,
                  "icon": "chevron-up",
                  "library": "lucide",
                  "fill": "$text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "UCTcS",
                  "name": "Expanded help label",
                  "fill": "$text",
                  "content": "How study works",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z9WJ3i",
              "name": "Study help body",
              "fill": "$text-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Answer each question once per session. Previous and Next retain your answers and feedback. Start a new study session, or open a question from Progress, to answer again. Earlier attempts and saved positions remain.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cOgTb",
          "name": "Distilled interface · shared behavior heading",
          "fill": "$text",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Distilled interface · shared behavior",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-20",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nz8G3",
          "name": "Status filters",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Progress and All questions combine bank-wide counts with the existing filters. Keep All → Not started → Needs review → Learning → Learned in reading and focus order. Counts remain bank-wide when filtering. Selected controls expose their state; counts are included in accessible names. Wrap controls for long German labels; retain at least 44 px targets. First use: All 310, Not started 310, remaining statuses 0.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nrR2c",
          "name": "Study and review order",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Study and completed review use context → German prompt → the 44 px English translation switch → translated prompt → any image → answer choices → feedback → navigation. German UI omits the translation control. Desktop study metadata stays compact above the prompt. How study works is collapsed by default after navigation; the expanded reference above specifies its contents. Expanding preserves focus, answers and saved position.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "b3xBL",
          "name": "Backup and confirmations",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Settings groups Download backup, file selection and its preview under Backup. Download is secondary while an import or file recovery awaits action. Preserve all backup/device comparison rows, the replacement warning, explicit confirmation and invalid-file recovery. Dialogs retain consequences, safe initial focus, Escape restoration and destructive-action styling.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xwtC2",
          "name": "Responsive and theme contract",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "All group descriptions and direct study paths remain visible. At widths or text sizes where progress and a study action cannot fit together, stack them in the same reading order. Keep 48 px group actions, 44 px translation/disclosure controls and visible focus rings. Count and percentage rules are unchanged. Use existing light/dark semantic colors; correctness and learning status retain text/icon cues.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": "$font-size-14",
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "i0NcJ",
          "name": "Localization for added labels",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "How study works → So funktioniert Lernen; Backup → Datensicherung. Combined German filters use the existing app vocabulary: Alle, Nicht begonnen, Wiederholen, In Bearbeitung and Gelernt, with counts. No new learning statuses or calculation rules. The translation switch remains absent in German UI.",
